  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "Executable Candidate binding of MiaAI-Lab's Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4-vLLM kit for one DGX Spark: Unsloth's Qwen3.6-35B-A3B NVFP4 checkpoint on stock vLLM 0.24.0 (ARM64 digest) with flashinfer attention, Marlin MoE, fastsafetensors loading, an auto-dtype KV cache, MTP speculative decoding with three tokens, prefix caching, up to four images per prompt, the qwen3 reasoning and qwen3_coder tool-call parsers, and the froggeric v20 chat template with thinking on. Upstream's README names the NVIDIA checkpoint but its start.sh (the executable truth) serves unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4, which is what is pinned. Code: no licence file upstream (README says MIT); model: Apache-2.0. Vonk physical Spark acceptance is pending. Security note: upstream allows the server to fetch images from any URL (--allowed-media-domains *). Anyone who can send requests to this endpoint can make the Spark fetch arbitrary URLs, including addresses on your local network.",
